1. Problem Statement
To develop a Flight Booking System using a Doubly Linked List in C++.
The system stores passenger booking information such as Booking ID, Passenger Name, Source, and Destination.
It allows users to book flights, display booking records in forward and backward directions, search for bookings, 
and cancel bookings dynamically using linked list operations. 
The project also demonstrates pointers and dynamic memory allocation functions such as malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), 
and free().

2. Approach: Flight Booking System Using Doubly Linked List
The Flight Booking System uses a Doubly Linked List to store and manage flight booking records dynamically.
Each node contains booking details and two pointers, prev and next,
which allow traversal in both forward and backward directions. y
The system supports booking, displaying, searching, and cancelling flights. 
It also demonstrates dynamic memory allocation using malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), and free().

